r status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKUYASU NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIHARA, YUSUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAYAMA, YOKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOGI, TOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUKEGAWA, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKUYASU, NOBORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A cylinder injection engine, in which fuel is injected directly into a combustion chamber, capable of suppressing the exhaustion of harmful component gas such as HC and increasing fuel efficiency by enabling a stratified combustion in an operating area ranging from a low speed range to a high speed range, wherein atomized fuel from a fuel injection nozzle is transported to an ignition plug by a tumble air flow which is produced in the combustion chamber and formed between the fuel injection nozzle disposed at the side part of the combustion chamber and the ignition plug disposed at the upper part of the combustion chamber, and the engine is formed so that fuel arrives at the ignition plug at the ignition timing of the ignition plug (tumble guide system cylinder injection engine).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un moteur à injection directe, dans lequel le carburant est injecté directement dans une chambre de combustion, capable de supprimer l'évacuation de composants gazeux dangereux, tels que les hydrocarbures, et d'augmenter l'efficacité du carburant par déclenchement d'une combustion stratifiée dans une zone de fonctionnement allant d'une plage faible vitesse à une plage grande vitesse. Le carburant atomisé en provenance d'un injecteur de carburant est transporté vers une bougie d'allumage par un flux d'air tourbillonnant produit dans la chambre de combustion et formé entre l'injecteur de carburant disposé dans la partie latérale de la chambre de combustion et la bougie d'allumage disposée dans la partie supérieure de la chambre de combustion. Le moteur est configuré de manière que le carburant arrive au niveau de la bougie d'allumage au calage de l'allumage de la bougie (moteur à injection directe à système de guidage du tourbillon).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>